    tsSyncedCursorRule draws the persistent RuleMark (web `<ReferenceLine x={syncedX}/>`).
  • cursorSync.ts external store → CursorSyncStore (@Observable replaces useSyncExternalStore) +
    CursorSyncReducer: setCursorSyncPosition (no-op when unchanged, delete on null),
    getCursorSyncPosition / useCursorSyncPosition(undefined→nil), clearCursorSync (absent→no-op),
    _resetCursorSyncStore → reset(). CursorSyncValue = .text|.number (null = Swift nil).
  • Real branches reproduced + tested: inside vs outside provider, cursor present vs absent,
    syncMethod index vs value, unmount clear, cross-chart broadcast over one store, per-syncId isolation.

